            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Gujarati for regular, then the Gujarati for everyday."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: શરૂ કરવું",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "શરૂ કરવું — śarū karvũ — \"to start, to begin\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "હું કાલે નવું કામ શરૂ કરીશ. — hũ kāle navũ kām śarū karīś — \"I will start a new job tomorrow.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "શરૂ કરવું (śarū karvũ) is built from śarū, \"begun\", and the inherited karvũ, \"to do\". Śarū is a loan from Arabic shurūʿ, \"a beginning\", through Persian, the word behind śarūāt (Lane)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for everyday life at A2."
            }
